onized vehicle capable of taking different forms including a motorcycle and a bipedal mech. The player takes control of one these three characters, utilizing the different forms of the Gunbike to traverse a series of enemy-filled, 3D stages. The objective is to complete each stage and to reach and defeat its boss before a meter, representing both a time limit and the player's health, runs out.", "summary": "Kahen Soukou Gunbike: Speed Power Gunbike, is an action video game released on April 23, 1998 exclusively in Japan for the PlayStation. It was the first game developed by Inti Creates and was published by Sony Music Entertainment Japan.", "themes": [{"id": 1, "name": "Action"}, {"id": 18, "name": "Science fiction"}], "url": "https://www.igdb.com/games/speed-power-gunbike", "videos": [{"id": 197776, "name": "Gameplay Video", "video_id": "nZkuKqmSPjI", "url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=nZkuKqmSPjI", "title": "Speed Power Gunbike (PS1) - Gameplay", "thumb": "https://i.ytimg.com/vi/nZkuKqmSPjI/hqdefault.jpg"}], "game_localizations": [{"id": 62265, "name": "\u53ef\u5909\u8d70\u653b \u30ac\u30f3\u30d0\u30a4\u30af", "cover": {"id": 606734, "url": "//images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_thumb/cod05q.jpg"}, "region": {"id": 3, "name": "Japan", "category": "locale", "identifier": "ja-JP"}}]}